{{!
  Table spec against the real database: @QuarkusTest with Dev Services (Testcontainers), the schema from the Flyway
  migrations. Each row goes in through the context's rows helper in its own transaction, so a refused row names the
  constraint that refused it; @AfterEach deletes what the tests left. Exemplar: application ordering OrderLineTableTest.
  Target: application/src/test/java/<package path>/persistence/<context>/<Name>TableTest.java
  Package: "package" is the file's own package (an application test has no layer suffix: com.example.application.
          persistence.ordering renders package com.example.application.persistence.ordering). scripts/scaffold.sh
          refuses a target outside the directory of the package the file declares.
  Vars:   package, Name, Rows (the context's rows helper with insert(em, entity), constraintOf(thrown) and
          deleteAll(em)), about (optional, the class comment: what the table holds to), imports (the entity classes,
          fully qualified), parents[type, name, row] (rows @BeforeEach inserts first, in order; row is a Java
          expression), refusals[test, first (optional, a row inserted before), row, constraint] (a row the database
          refuses, and the constraint that refuses it), readBack (optional) {test, Entity, row, key (the find key, a
          Java expression over stored), columns[getter, expected]}
  Expressions use triple braces so generics and quotes are not HTML-escaped.
}}
